<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14926" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρειά</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰρ]</span>, 
			Ion.
		 and poet. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρειή</span></b> ,
			ἡ, collective noun, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>menaces, threats,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λευγαλέοις ἐπέεσσιν . . καὶ ἀρειῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					20.109
				</span></i>
			, but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μειλιχίοις ἐπέεσσιν . . καὶ ἀρειῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					21.339
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολλὰ δὲ μειλιχίοισι . . πολλὰ δ᾽
					ἀρειῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					17.431
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
